Subject: register VM: deferred reference counting zero-count table (stage D2)

What this does:
  Stage D2 of the deferred-RC plan
  (`HP-S3-DEFERRED-RC-PLAN-2026-10-02.md` section 3) turns the collector on.
  Register-VM frames are already published as GC root ranges (D1); D2 makes a
  counted value whose ref_count reaches zero park on a zero-count table (ZCT)
  instead of being freed, and adds the reconcile pass that frees only the parked
  values no live register refers to. Registers still own their values at this
  stage, so the table is expected to stay small; the point is to validate the
  machinery before D4 makes register stores stop owning.

  Concretely:
  - `JSMallocBlockHeader` gains `in_zct : 1` (the `gc_obj_type` field narrows
    from 6 to 5 bits; the bit lives in the same byte as `mark`/`gc_notrace`).
  - `JSRuntime` gains the ZCT (`zct`, `zct_len`, `zct_cap`, `zct_nobj`,
    `zct_limit`, `drc_in_reconcile`). The table is grown with the raw
    `rt->mf.js_realloc` (never `js_realloc_rt`) so pushing a value can never
    trigger a GC, and is released with the matching `rt->mf.js_free`.
  - `js_free_value_rt` parks a value at zero instead of freeing it: objects and
    function bytecodes move to `gc_zero_ref_count_list`; every other counted
    type is appended to `rt->zct`.
  - `js_drc_pin` / `js_drc_unpin` add and remove the register-window references,
    and `js_drc_reconcile_locked` frees the parked values no register holds.
    `JS_RunGC` runs pin, reconcile, the existing cycle collector, then unpin, so
    a register-only object has a count of at least one while the collector runs.
  - Safepoints (`js_drc_safepoint`, a cheap check against `zct_limit`) run from
    `__js_poll_interrupts` and when `JS_Call` returns to C with no JS frame;
    `JS_FreeRuntime` reconciles and drops the table before its list assertions.

  The public behaviour is unchanged: the differential suite, the box2d
  checksum, the leak assertion and the ASan/UBSan runs are all clean.

  Measured cost on `.local/box2d-gap/fixed.js` (interleaved `perf stat -r5`
  against the same tree built with `-DQJS_DRC=0`): about +0.18G instructions
  and +2.6% cycles. That is above the plan's soft gate of +0.10G but well below
  its +0.3G abort threshold, and it is the deferred-free bookkeeping
  (park + reconcile) rather than the safepoint or pin walk, which the counters
  show run only ~2k / ~14k register slots over the whole benchmark. D4 removes
  the register-release traffic that dominates this cost, so it is carried as a
  known stage-D2 overhead rather than optimised here.

  Also fixes the validator build guard: the `js_drc_validate_roots` call in
  `JS_RunGC` is now compiled only when `QJS_REGVM` is on, matching the
  function's own guard, so a `QJS_DRC_VALIDATE` build of the plain stack
  interpreter compiles.

